!results/
!results/*.log
# ...and the audit logs one level down.  `!results/*.log` does not reach results/audit/, which is
# where every measurement queue actually writes, so those logs were untracked all day and four
# container rewinds took them: mix40.log at 74 of 80 runs, rep722.log after all twelve had
# finished, and twice before that.  The numbers survived only because they had been copied by
# hand into the .md files beside them.  A measurement that is not committed did not happen.
!results/audit/
!results/audit/*.log
# THE SAME BUG, THE SAME DAY, ONE DIRECTORY OVER.  The note above is about results/audit/; the
# measurement sweeps for the report write to results/stage2/ and results/train2/, and `!results/*.log`
# does not reach them either.  Forty final-round runs sat untracked through a container restart.
# Every directory a sweep writes to has to be named here, not just the first one that bit us.
!results/stage2/
!results/stage2/*.log
!results/train2/
!results/train2/*.log
