# Every arm mkbase.py generates.  They are outputs, not sources: the builder is versioned and
# each queue rebuilds its own arms before running them, so a committed copy is a stale duplicate
# that can silently disagree with the builder it came from.  myalg_orig.py is the exception --
# it is the pinned input -- and it is matched by none of these.
myalg_div*.py
myalg_wd*.py
myalg_hm*.py
myalg_fo*.py
myalg_brk*.py
myalg_ops.py
myalg_q*.py
myalg_s*.py

# Stray queue marker.  chain.sh runs its stages from harness/, so a stage's own
# `echo <name> > "$(dirname "$0")/CURRENT"` -- correct when it is launched as
# harness/x.sh from recon/ -- resolves to ./CURRENT here instead.  harness/CURRENT keeps
# saying `chain`, which is what a restart should resume, so the effect is right and the
# file is litter.  chain.sh invokes by full path once it is not mid-run.
/CURRENT

# Staging tree for harness/rebuild.sh: freshly built .so plus symlinks back to this
# directory, so the new build can be run against the old one before anything is
# installed.  Regenerable from ogc_fast.cpp, which is tracked; the validated binaries
# are committed in place, not from here.
/build_new/
